{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$i=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'kibitz-runs\\\\2026-09-02-still-in-peer\\\\r2\\\\input.md' | ForEach-Object { \"'$i++; '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f \"'$i, $_ }'","aggregated_output":"    1: # Driver anchor -- item 2, the still-in LAB PEER for the AnimateDiff v3 lane (2026-09-02)\r\n    2: \r\n    3: Campaign: `docs/2026-09-02-animatediff-ledger-experiments/` (PROBLEM_STATEMENT.md, fresh-eyes/,\r\n    4: instrument/). Judged order: (0) the instrument -- CODED and merged 2026-09-02 (969f2578, dc4beea5);\r\n    5: (1) the adapter sweep -- running; **(2) this item**; (3) pack language under the 77-token budget;\r\n    6: (4) one timeline per shot. This anchor is the driver's code-grounded position BEFORE the panel;\r\n    7: the four readers' fact digest it rests on is reproduced in section 2 with file:line.\r\n    8: \r\n    9: Operator rulings that bind this item, verbatim where recorded:\r\n   10: * \"it is paramount that the prompting for this new AnimateDiff workflow must obey the visual\r\n   11:   style ... I think we lost the visual style.\" (PROBLEM_STATEMENT 5B)\r\n   12: * \"anime is not the only target; all visual styles need to craft the episode as well when\r\n   13:   selected.\" (GO_FORWARD_PLAN 1.14, 2026-09-02 evening)\r\n   14: * \"always remember when adding a new video pack to follow the preflight video guide\" --\r\n   15:   `docs/VIDEO_LANE_PREFLIGHT.md` gates 1-8 + `tests/test_lane_preflight_matrix.py` BEFORE the id\r\n   16:   is registered or a profile names it.\r\n   17: * No damping words in motion prompts; flicker is a recipe problem, never a wording one; story\r\n   18:   quality is done; every arm is an ADDITION judged against the shipped recipe with a same-seed\r\n   19:   A/A null first; recipes are hard-won and never traded for VRAM or speed.\r\n   20: \r\n   21: ## 1. What the item is, in one paragraph\r\n   22: \r\n   23: A NEW engine id beside the shipping `animatediff15_v3_haunted_video`, subclassing it, that renders\r\n   24: the same recipe (v3 module + adapter, 20 / 8.0 / euler / normal, 512x288 hold-2, static 16/4\r\n   25: pyramid, the live negative) but starts the sampler from a STILL instead of an empty latent. The\r\n   26: still is the lane's own **in-family plate**: one 512x288 frame minted in the same graph from the\r\n   27: same SD1.5 checkpoint with the adapter at 0.0, prompted with the style pack's full language and\r\n   28: the ledger's setting, palette and lighting, then VAE-encoded, repeated to the sampler batch and\r\n   29: sampled at denoise < 1.0 (E1). The plate carries the STYLE into every frame at the pixel level,\r\n   30: which the two-word cue cannot; the motion recipe is untouched. ADE image injection (E2) is a\r\n   31: later knob behind its own VRAM probe. Nothing about the shipping engine, its graph, its tests,\r\n   32: its receipt id or the 4060 provisioning set moves.\r\n   33: \r\n   34: ## 2. Code facts the design rests on (readers 2026-09-02, verified file:line)\r\n   35: \r\n   36: **The registry contract and the gates a new lane owes.**\r\n   37: * Registration is `@register` + a unique `name` (`nodes/_otr_shared/engine_registry_base.py:141-150`);\r\n   38:   the pack's own gates then demand a `CAPABILITIES` row (`registry.py:273-275, 688-721`), an explicit\r\n   39:   `accepts_still`, a declared `still_plan` tuple (`()` valid), exactly one live menu option\r\n   40:   (`exact_menu_option_for`), and a row in the generated `docs/ENGINE_MATRIX.md`\r\n   41:   (`tests/test_lane_preflight_matrix.py:940-964`, `tests/test_engine_matrix_doc.py:43-49`).\r\n   42: * The preflight suite iterates `all_engine_names()` with `EXPECTED_RED` empty, so registration IS\r\n   43:   the gate (`test_lane_preflight_matrix.py:176-273, 383-393`). Files a new lane touches for the\r\n   44:   matrix to pass: `eng_<name>.py`, `registry.py` (CAPABILITIES), `_otr_video_engines/__init__.py`\r\n   45:   (guarded import), `scripts/build_video_evidence_manifest.py` (a >= 6-word `admission_unenforced`\r\n   46:   sentence, then regenerate the manifest -- never hand-edit it), `docs/ENGINE_MATRIX.md`\r\n   47:   (`tools/engine_matrix.py`), and a `tests/test_<lane>.py` naming the id AND its exact canvas\r\n   48:   (G2.2 pin, `:627-636, 711-731`). G8 (the solo smoke) is the only live gate and is prose-only\r\n   49:   (`docs/VIDEO_LANE_PREFLIGHT.md:234-243`).\r\n   50: * A sibling of an existing lane also owes the G1.3 per-artifact CLASS attributes with byte floors\r\n   51:   below and within 15% of the real files (`tests/test_ghost_signal_peers.py:106-127`).\r\n   52: \r\n   53: **The shipping lane's seams.**\r\n   54: * `GhostSignalV3HauntedEngine` is the only registered Ghost engine; base classes are unregistered\r\n   55:   and their ids tombstoned (`eng_ghost_signal_official.py:68-175`). The graph is built INLINE in\r\n   56:   `render_clip` (`eng_ghost_signal.py:781-970`) from a closed `GHOST_NODE_CANDIDATES` dict of seven\r\n   57:   classes (`:154-162`); `ADE_ADE_OMITTED_SOCKETS` pins `sample_settings` and friends as OMITTED\r\n   58:   (`:166-172`); tests pin 7 resolver names, 8 executed node instances on the haunted lane, the\r\n   59:   omitted sockets, `sampler_inputs.latent == 'EmptyLatentImage'`, `init_image is None`, and\r\n   60:   `model_artifacts` == [checkpoint, motion_module, adapter] (`tests/test_ghost_signal_lane.py:226-243,\r\n   61:   416-520`; `tests/test_ghost_signal_haunted.py:165-172`; `tests/test_render_receipts.py:129-143`).\r\n   62:   => the peer is a NEW subclass that overrides `name`, `recipe_receipt_id`, `_node_candidates`,\r\n   63:   `render_clip`, `sampler_inputs_for`, `model_artifacts`, `session_identity`, `shot_cache_identity`;\r\n   64:   it never edits the shipping class.\r\n   65: * `_build_render_request` reads only shot/request ids, text_prompt, negative_prompt,\r\n   66:   timing.target_frame_count and seed_bundle.request_seed (`eng_ghost_signal.py:732-778`); the seed\r\n   67:   is `_seed_from_hash(render_request_hash, shot_id)` and does not move when a still, a denoise or an\r\n   68:   adapter strength is added (`render_driver.py:548-553, 3768-3772`) -- same-seed A/Bs stay valid.\r\n   69: * `GHOST_CHECKPOINT_NAME` is a module constant read inside methods (`:411, 535-536, 715, 466, 497`),\r\n   70:   not a class seam; the peer keeps the checkpoint, so this stays a note (promote to a class seam\r\n   71:   only when a per-style checkpoint arm E11 is opened).\r\n   72: * `prepare()` runs only the `ckpt` node and registers the base MODEL patcher; STAGE 2 encodes the\r\n   73:   two prompts and releases the CLIP; STAGE 3 builds context -> lora -> ADE loader -> EmptyLatentImage\r\n   74:   -> KSampler; STAGE 4 decodes with the external `vae` handle (`eng_ghost_signal.py:678-729,\r\n   75:   849-945`). `run_graph` accepts `external_results` as legal Wire sources (`wrapper_bridge.py:460-560`).\r\n   76:   The plain checkpoint MODEL stays usable beside the ADE-cloned one (ADE clones,\r\n   77:   `ADE nodes_gen1.py:85`), so a single-frame plate branch on `Wire('base_model')` is legal in the\r\n   78:   same STAGE 3 graph.\r\n   79: * No image node (LoadImage, VAEEncode, ImageScale, RepeatLatentBatch, LatentFromBatch) is in the\r\n   80:   lane's Phase-0 `/object_info` capture (`docs/2026-08-22-ghost-signal-object-info.json` holds the\r\n   81:   seven shipping classes); the peer needs its own live capture before pinning any class id -- ONE\r\n   82:   NAME PER ALIAS, no probing at render time.\r\n   83: \r\n   84: **How a still reaches an engine today, and why the peer does not go that way first.**\r\n   85: * A still reaches an engine ONLY as `request['asset_refs']['init_image']` (`render_driver.py:342-380,\r\n   86:   4389-4410`); `render_driver` joins the beat's SCENE still when the family is image_to_video /\r\n   87:   static_motion or `init_image` is in `required_inputs` (`:2240-2275, 1307-1313`), and raises\r\n   88:   `DeferredImageGapError` with no portrait fallback when the row is missing. Whether the image\r\n   89:   phase MINTS anything is `engine_consumes_still` = `accepts_still` (`otr_image_gen_dispatcher.py:640-657`).\r\n   90:   Scene stills are 1472x832 from a foreign image family (`otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:471-484`).\r\n   91: * The lane is in `_NO_STILL_VIDEO_ENGINES` (`scripts/otr_provision.py:1546-1551`) precisely so the\r\n   92:   8 GB box is not gated on the ~11 GB Klein bundle (PROBLEM_STATEMENT 7; judgment 1.2). A peer that\r\n   93:   flips `accepts_still=True` would be pulled out of that set on the 4060 unless its id is excluded\r\n   94:   by hand, and would have to declare the G3.7-scoped ownership fields differently\r\n   95:   (`test_lane_preflight_matrix.py:1036-1038`).\r\n   96: * The receipt already hashes `still_sha256` from `asset_refs.init_image` content\r\n   97:   (`render_driver.py:4095, 4132`); an engine-minted plate is NOT on `asset_refs`, so the peer\r\n   98:   must put the plate's identity into `sampler_inputs` itself (section 4.5).\r\n   99: \r\n  100: **Conditioning mechanics available on this install (ComfyUI 0.34.3, ADE 1.6.0).**\r\n  101: * Stock init-latent path: `VAEEncode(pixels, vae)`; `RepeatLatentBatch(amount <= 64)`\r\n  102:   (`ComfyUI/nodes.py:1304-1330`); `LatentFromBatch(samples, batch_index, length)`; `KSampler.denoise`\r\n  103:   0-1. `ADE_UpscaleAndVAEEncode(image, vae, latent_size, scale_method, crop)` resizes + encodes in\r\n  104:   one node (`animatediff/nodes_animatelcmi2v.py:133-159`). `VHS_DuplicateLatents` exists\r\n  105:   (`comfyui-videohelpersuite`) but VHS is NOT in `otr_provision.py`'s pinned set -- not a dependency\r\n  106:   the peer may take.\r\n  107: * Ghost source batch = `max(ceil(T / 2), 16)` latents with `max_frames = 0` (`eng_ghost_signal.py:\r\n  108:   201-211, 385-392`): a beat over 128 delivered frames needs more than one RepeatLatentBatch.\r\n  109: * `ADE_NoisedImageInjection` needs `ADE_AnimateDiffSamplingSettings` on the loader's\r\n  110:   `sample_settings` socket (the socket the shipping lane pins OMITTED) and decodes + re-encodes the\r\n  111:   WHOLE batch through the VAE at each injection point (`animatediff/sampling.py:645-693`) -- E2 is\r\n  112:   a second arm behind a VRAM probe, exactly as the judgment ordered.\r\n  113: * ComfyUI-Advanced-ControlNet is not installed; SparseCtrl (E7) stays deferred.\r\n  114: \r\n  115: **Stills, layout, style packs.**\r\n  116: * Episode stills live at `<output>/otr/episodes/<episode_id>/stills/{object_id}_{hash12}.png`,\r\n  117:   with a `stills_manifest.json` beside them (`nodes/_otr_shared/portrait_ledger.py:63-108`,\r\n  118:   `otr_image_gen_dispatcher.py:2099-2139`). The replay bundle freezes `stills/` and `portraits/`\r\n  119:   whole (`scripts/otr_freeze_replay_bundle.py`, FROZEN_DIRS).\r\n  120: * A planned shot carries `ghost_prompt` (with `mode` in figure / object / signal and the bookend),\r\n  121:   `beat_id`, `role`, `char_id`, `subject_sigil` -- no still path (`otr_shot_lock.py:1662-1690`).\r\n  122:   `GHOST_CHARACTER_CYCLE = ('figure','object','figure','signal')` (`ghost_signal_author.py:101,\r\n  123:   472-505`).\r\n  124: * Packs: nine files under `nodes/visual_styles/` (+ the run-time `visual_storybased`); prompt\r\n  125:   LANGUAGE only -- `positive_tail`, `image_grade_tail`, `broadcast_tail`, `era_tail`,\r\n  126:   `negative_tail`, eleven look strings incl. `plate_look`, `scene_instruction_look`,\r\n  127:   `portrait_look`, four dicts (`_otr_visual_styles.py:559-618`; PROBLEM_STATEMENT 154-162).\r\n  128:   The video cue is `compact_style_cue()` = two words (`_otr_visual_styles.py:632-653`); the leaf\r\n  129:   validator bans medium/camera/quality words -- \"style is Python's job on this lane\"\r\n  130:   (`ghost_signal_author.py:316-330`); the finalizer enforces one 77-token window and 320 chars on\r\n  131:   BOTH prompts (`:1348-1367`).\r\n  132: \r\n  133: ## 3. Decisions (the driver's position; the panel pressure-tests these)\r\n  134: \r\n  135: **D1. A new lane, id `animatediff15_v3_stillin_lab_video`, menu label \"AnimateDiff v3 still-in lab\r\n  136: (512x288)\", recipe receipt `animatediff_sd15_v3_haunted_stillin_e1_512x288_lab_v1`.** Subclass of\r\n  137: `GhostSignalV3HauntedEngine`; every G1.3 constant a class attribute it inherits or overrides;\r\n  138: `status: lab` in its profile; 5080 only until measured. The word \"lab\" is in the id on purpose:\r\n  139: it is never a default, never in a shipping profile, and its receipt id can never be mistaken for\r\n  140: the shipping one.\r\n  141: \r\n  142: **D2. The plate is minted IN-GRAPH by the peer, not taken from the image phase.** Consequences,\r\n  143: all deliberate: `accepts_still` stays `False`, `required_inputs` stays `('text_prompt',)`,\r\n  144: `still_plan` stays `()`, `subject_ownership` stays `'prompt'`, the id stays OUT of any dispatcher\r\n  145: minting and is added to `_NO_STILL_VIDEO_ENGINES` alongside its parent so the 4060 is never gated\r\n  146: on an image bundle by it. The plate is a recipe cell of the VIDEO lane, hashed by its receipt, not\r\n  147: an asset of the image phase. The dispatcher-fed still (portrait-derived `scene_character` at\r\n  148: 1472x832 through `resolve_aspect_transform`, `motion_common.py:135-166`) is arm E1b, a LATER knob\r\n  149: on the same peer, opened only after E1a is judged; it is the one that would need\r\n  150: `accepts_still=True` and its own provisioning exclusion, and it is not built now.\r\n  151: \r\n  152: **D3. Plate prompt = the pack's language, the ledger's world, never the leaf.** Positive:\r\n  153: `<positive_tail>. <plate_look or scene_instruction_look>. <setting phrase from the ledger:\r\n  154: place, era, palette, lighting>. <mode subject>` measured by `measure_clip_tokens` to <= 77 with\r\n  155: the pack clauses first (they are the point) and the ledger phrase trimmed last; negative = the\r\n  156: composed lane negative (`LANE_HYGIENE_NEGATIVE` + pack `effective_negative`). NO character name,\r\n  157: no dialogue, no camera words, no lettering: the plate owns MEDIUM and WORLD; motion and framing\r\n  158: stay with the video prompt (mode law) exactly as today. The plate branch runs with the adapter at\r\n  159: 0.0 (plain checkpoint MODEL): the plate is the pristine image-domain picture of the style, the\r\n  160: adapter then haunts the motion on top of it.\r\n  161: \r\n  162: **D4. Mode routing by `ghost_prompt.mode`, not a frozen cycle.** The plan's one-liner (\"cycle\r\n  163: frozen to figure\") predates the r2/r3 folds that preferred routing; the plate makes routing free:\r\n  164: figure -> a figure plate (a person of the character's described build in the world, no name),\r\n  165: object -> the object with no person, signal -> the environment with no person, bookend ->\r\n  166: `scene_open`. Freezing the cycle would change the shipping author's schedule for the peer only and\r\n  167: hide a variable; routing keeps the schedule identical between the two lanes so the A/B isolates\r\n  168: the still. GO_FORWARD_PLAN 1.14's one-liner is corrected in this change.\r\n  169: \r\n  170: **D5. E1 mechanics, stock nodes only.** STAGE 3 gains, before the sampler:\r\n  171: `plate_latent = EmptyLatentImage{512x288, 1}` -> `plate_sampler = KSampler{model: Wire('base_model'),\r\n  172: seed: plate_seed, steps 20, cfg 8.0, euler, normal, denoise 1.0, positive: plate_positive, negative:\r\n  173: negative}` -> `plate_decode = VAEDecode{vae}` (the plate PNG is written to\r\n  174: `<episode>/stills/plate_<shot_id>_<sha12>.png` for the record, section D7) -> `plate_encode =\r\n  175: VAEEncode{pixels, vae}` -> `repeat = RepeatLatentBatch{amount: min(U, 64)}` (+ a second\r\n  176: `RepeatLatentBatch` and `LatentFromBatch{0, U}` when `U > 64`; U = the lane's `source_request`) ->\r\n  177: `sampler.latent_image`, with `sampler.denoise = 0.75` (class attribute `E1_DENOISE`, sweep 0.6 /\r\n  178: 0.75 / 0.9 later; 0.9 only if motion is damped). The plate prompt is a THIRD CLIPTextEncode in\r\n  179: STAGE 2 before the CLIP is released. Node candidates: the seven shipping classes + `VAEEncode`,\r\n  180: `RepeatLatentBatch`, `LatentFromBatch` (one name per alias, pinned from a fresh live capture).\r\n  181: Resize policy: none needed -- the plate is minted at the canvas. `ADE_UpscaleAndVAEEncode` and\r\n  182: `VHS_DuplicateLatents` are rejected: the first is an ADE-private helper for a foreign-size still\r\n  183: (E1b's problem, not E1a's), the second is an unprovisioned dependency.\r\n  184: \r\n  185: **D6. The seed.** `plate_seed = (request_seed * 1000003 + 0x5EED) & 0x7FFFFFFF` -- derived, so a\r\n  186: same-ledger replay reproduces the plate by construction and a changed request seed changes it; the\r\n  187: video sampler keeps `request_seed` untouched so the shipping lane and the peer share the video\r\n  188: seed on the same ledger (the A/B isolates the init latent).\r\n  189: \r\n  190: **D7. Reproducibility and the record.** The plate is deterministic from (checkpoint, plate prompt,\r\n  191: plate seed, canvas, steps/cfg/sampler) on one box, and the peer ALSO writes it to\r\n  192: `<episode>/stills/plate_<shot_id>_<sha12>.png` and records `plate_sha256` on the clip -- so the\r\n  193: replay bundle carries the exact frame, `otr_verify_replay.py` can compare plate hashes across the\r\n  194: A/A, and a bitwise-unstable GPU kernel shows up as a plate-hash disagreement rather than as an\r\n  195: unexplained video difference. The peer does not READ the file back on a replay in the first build\r\n  196: (the plate is re-minted; the hash is the check) -- reading it back is a second knob if the null\r\n  197: proves noisy.\r\n  198: \r\n  199: **D8. The receipt (the r4 pin, applied to the peer).** `sampler_inputs_for` returns the parent's\r\n  200: dict plus `latent: 'VAEEncode'`, `init_image: <plate_sha256>`, `denoise: E1_DENOISE`, `plate_seed`,\r\n  201: `plate_prompt`, `plate_negative`, `plate_steps/cfg/sampler/scheduler`, `plate_adapter_strength: 0.0`,\r\n  202: `repeat_amount: U`; `model_artifacts` is the parent's (no new weight). Two A/A replays agree by\r\n  203: construction (every field derives from the ledger + seed); a changed plate prompt, denoise, seed\r\n  204: or canvas disagrees. `session_identity` / `shot_cache_identity` gain the plate sha so a cache hit\r\n  205: can never hand a still-free render to the peer.\r\n  206: \r\n  207: **D9. The proof.** All legs on the canonical graph, published to `otr/obs/`, clean runner, no\r\n  208: harness title (the 17:45 lesson), engine selected per role by a `lab` profile\r\n  209: `otr_stillin_lab_5080.json` (copy of the haunted profile with the three video roles on the peer,\r\n  210: `status: lab`, variants regenerated). Sequence:\r\n  211: 1. G8 solo smoke on one beat: canvas probed 512x288, frame count exact, silence probed, VRAM peak\r\n  212:    receipted (the plate branch adds one 512x288 single-frame sample and one VAE encode; expected\r\n  213:    well under the lane's 13.3-14.2 GB peak -- MEASURED, not assumed).\r\n  214: 2. Same-ledger A/B per style via the replay mode: freeze one episode rendered on the SHIPPING lane\r\n  215:    (anime), replay it on the peer; repeat for `storybook_engraving` and `paper_origami` (three\r\n  216:    styles, two non-anime). Each pair carries its A/A null (the peer replayed twice).\r\n  217: 3. Verdict, in the operator's words: \"looks like <the selected style>\", stills and video the same\r\n  218:    show, name / gender / portrait / voice agreeing -- judged as radio drama, by his eye, with the\r\n  219:    render trace to attribute any difference.\r\n  220: Stop the item if the null is not a null (plate hashes or seeds differ across two replays), or if\r\n  221: E1 at 0.75 damps motion visibly on all three styles (then 0.9 is tried once; a second failure ends\r\n  222: E1 and opens E2's probe).\r\n  223: \r\n  224: **D10. Not in this item.** E2 (image injection) and its VRAM probe; E1b (dispatcher-fed still);\r\n  225: E7 (SparseCtrl, pack not installed); per-style checkpoints; any change to the shipping engine,\r\n  226: its graph, tests, receipt, or the 4060 provisioning set; any prompt change on the video prompt\r\n  227: (that is item 3).\r\n  228: \r\n  229: ## 4. The build list (what one window codes after r4)\r\n  230: \r\n  231: 1. `nodes/_otr_video_engines/eng_ghost_signal_stillin_lab.py`: `GhostSignalV3StillInLabEngine(\r\n  232:    GhostSignalV3HauntedEngine)` with `name`, `recipe_receipt_id`, `E1_DENOISE = 0.75`,\r\n  233:    `PLATE_*` class constants, `_node_candidates()` (ten names), `render_clip()` (STAGE 2 with the\r\n  234:    plate prompt, STAGE 3 with the plate branch), `_plate_prompt(request, vstyle, ledger_world)`,\r\n  235:    `_plate_seed(request_seed)`, `sampler_inputs_for`, `session_identity`, `shot_cache_identity`,\r\n  236:    `canonicalize` adding `plate_sha256` to the clip (schemas.py: one new optional key, since\r\n  237:    `CanonicalClip` is `extra='forbid'`).\r\n  238: 2. `registry.py` CAPABILITIES row (copy of the haunted row, `status: lab`); `__init__.py` guarded\r\n  239:    import; `scripts/otr_provision.py` `_ANIMATEDIFF_ENGINES` gains the id (so it stays no-still on\r\n  240:    the 4060); `scripts/build_video_evidence_manifest.py` sentence + regenerate;\r\n  241:    `tools/engine_matrix.py` regenerate `docs/ENGINE_MATRIX.md`.\r\n  242: 3. `config/profiles/otr_stillin_lab_5080.json` + `scripts/build_variants.py --all/--check`.\r\n  243: 4. Tests: `tests/test_ghost_signal_stillin_lab.py` (canvas pin, node candidates, exactly N node\r\n  244:    instances, `sampler_inputs` pins, plate-seed derivation, plate-prompt budget <= 77 on all nine\r\n  245:    packs, no name / camera / lettering word in any plate prompt, `session_identity` moves with the\r\n  246:    plate sha); `test_render_receipts.py` gains the \"plate changes the sha\" case; the preflight\r\n  247:    matrix and `test_ghost_signal_peers.py` floors run green.\r\n  248: 5. A `docs/evidence/lane_receipts/animatediff15_v3_stillin_lab_video.md` G8 receipt after the smoke.\r\n  249: \r\n  250: ## 5. Open questions for the panel (r1)\r\n  251: \r\n  252: * Q1. Is the in-graph plate (D2) the right FIRST build, or should E1b (dispatcher still) go first\r\n  253:   because it reuses the existing still spine? The driver says D2: it isolates the style variable,\r\n  254:   needs no image model, cannot gate the 4060, and cannot pull a foreign-family look into the lane.\r\n  255: * Q2. The plate prompt's ledger phrase: is \"setting, era, palette, lighting\" the right slice of the\r\n  256:   ledger, and which existing composer (the still lane's scene prompt builder in\r\n  257:   `otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py`) should the peer borrow from rather than write new prose?\r\n  258: * Q3. `denoise 0.75` first -- or 0.6, given the adapter at 1.0 already pulls toward its domain?\r\n  259: * Q4. Should the plate be minted at the adapter's LIVE strength instead of 0.0 (the plate would\r\n  260:   already carry the haunt)? The driver says 0.0: the plate is the style's own picture; the adapter\r\n  261:   is a motion-domain knob and the sweep is measuring it separately.\r\n  262: * Q5. Mode routing (D4) versus the plan's frozen cycle -- any reason routing hides a variable?\r\n  263: * Q6. Anything in `render_driver`'s coverage / jump-still / segment path that assumes an\r\n  264:   EmptyLatentImage lane and would break a subclass that repeats latents (multi-segment beats,\r\n  265:   `U > 64`)?\r\n  266: \r\n  267: ## 6. r1 fold (Fable 5.1 cold read + Antigravity `agy` Gemini 3.8 Flash (High); judgment in `kibitz-runs/2026-09-02-still-in-peer/r1/judgment.md`)\r\n  268: \r\n  269: The two reviews split on the still source. Antigravity: reverse D2 to the dispatcher still\r\n  270: (identity continuity, unity with the episode's portraits; \"the 4060 justification contradicts\r\n  271: D1\"). Fable: keep the in-graph plate (on an all-Ghost policy the dispatcher mints nothing, so\r\n  272: \"reuse the still\" is a new image phase; at denoise 0.75 SD1.5 repaints the medium and an init\r\n  273: survives as layout, palette, lighting). What decided it is a document neither the anchor nor\r\n  274: the 09-02 judgment had folded: **`docs/SPEC_haunted_image_to_video.md` (2026-08-30) already\r\n  275: took this lane through r1 (Antigravity) and r2 (Codex)** and closed on two findings, both\r\n  276: re-confirmed at the file today:\r\n  277: \r\n  278: 1. **Route A -- a still VAE-encoded and repeated as the init latent -- plausibly fails BY\r\n  279:    CONSTRUCTION**: identical cross-frame keys in the motion module's temporal attention\r\n  280:    suppress the trajectory while high-frequency texture boils. So Route A is a PROBE, not a\r\n  281:    build: denoise 0.35 / 0.50 / 0.65 / 0.80, disqualified if <= 0.50 shows no macro-motion with\r\n  282:    texture boil, or >= 0.65 loses the still within 2-3 frames. The mechanism is the same\r\n  283:    whichever still is fed, which makes the still SOURCE a secondary question for the probe.\r\n  284: 2. **Upstream recommends the animated image come from the SAME SD1.5 model used for\r\n  285:    animation**; a Z-Image still into a haunted SD1.5 checkpoint invites cross-model drift\r\n  286:    (spec 11.5). This is the in-family plate's strongest reason, and it replaces the 4060\r\n  287:    reasoning the anchor gave.\r\n  288: \r\n  289: The 08-30 spec's own recommendation (\"measure the image phase on the 4060 first, qualify\r\n  290: Advanced-ControlNet, build SparseCtrl\") is superseded by the 09-02 campaign order, which\r\n  291: deferred SparseCtrl (E7: a new pack pin, 1.99 GB, 323 MB of overnight headroom) and put the\r\n  292: still-in probe here. Its Route A probe grid and disqualification rule are adopted verbatim.\r\n  293: CLAUDE.md 0A forbids a standalone stock-node probe graph, so the probe VEHICLE is the lab\r\n  294: peer itself rendering canonical episodes with a denoise knob, published to `otr/obs/`.\r\n  295: \r\n  296: ## 7. Revised decisions after r1 (what r2 plans the code for)\r\n  297: \r\n  298: **D1 (id, receipt, lab status) -- unchanged.** `animatediff15_v3_stillin_lab_video`,\r\n  299: recipe `animatediff_sd15_v3_haunted_stillin_e1_512x288_lab_v1`, `status: lab`, 5080 only,\r\n  300: never a default, never a tombstoned id (`public_engines.py:398-402`).\r\n  301: \r\n  302: **D2 (in-family plate) -- STANDS, reasoning replaced.** The plate is minted in-graph from the\r\n  303: same checkpoint because (a) upstream says the animated image should come from the animating\r\n  304: model, (b) it needs no image phase (on 8 GB the image role is a native abort,\r\n  305: PBUG-20260829-03; on the 5080 it is a cost the probe does not need to pay), and (c) it is the\r\n  306: cheapest vehicle for the Route A probe, whose outcome is the same for either still source.\r\n  307: `accepts_still` stays `False`, `required_inputs` `('text_prompt',)`, `still_plan` `()`,\r\n  308: `subject_ownership` `'prompt'`, `prompt_profile` stays `GHOST_PROMPT_PROFILE` (or ShotLock\r\n  309: stamps no `ghost_prompt` and render falls to v1, `otr_shot_lock.py:2137, 2246-2247`); the id\r\n  310: joins `_ANIMATEDIFF_ENGINES` (`otr_provision.py:1516-1522`) so it stays in the no-still set.\r\n  311: **E1b (dispatcher still, `accepts_still=True`, the 08-30 spec's contract corrected to\r\n  312: `required_inputs=('text_prompt','init_image')` and a truthful non-empty `still_plan`) is the\r\n  313: SECOND engine id, opened only if Route A survives the probe.**\r\n  314: \r\n  315: **D3 (plate prompt) -- replaced by the plate-prompt composer, modelled on\r\n  316: `_compose_background_plate_prompt` (`otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1839-1865`).** Protected\r\n  317: head, in order: the FULL `positive_tail` (never `compact_style_cue` / `prefix_style_cue`,\r\n  318: `_otr_visual_styles.py:632-685` -- that IS the defect), `plate_look`, `_read_setting` top-2\r\n  319: (`:40-49`), `get_era_tail(profile=\"still\")` (`_otr_story_brief_helpers.py:321-341`, capped\r\n  320: 120 chars). Droppable in fixed order: `era_tail`, `image_grade_tail`, atmosphere terms, the\r\n  321: second setting term. NEVER: `scene_instruction_look` (an instruction sentence),\r\n  322: `broadcast_tail`, any `motion_registers` entry (camera words; storybook's carry \"gently\" --\r\n  323: a damping word), `open_subjects` / `announcer_*` / `portrait_*` (subject, identity), the leaf,\r\n  324: the mode law, `NO_TEXT_CLAUSE`. Negative: the request's own composed Ghost negative\r\n  325: (`ghost_signal_prompt.py:622-651`), verbatim. Budget: COUNTED with `measure_clip_tokens`\r\n  326: (`ghost_signal_author.py:1234-1249`), `GhostBudgetError` if the protected head exceeds 69,\r\n  327: pinned by a test over all nine packs plus a synthetic long `visual_storybased`. **The\r\n  328: composition lives in `render_driver`'s Ghost branch (where `_vstyle` and ledger meta exist,\r\n  329: `:2881-2950`) as a declared optional `VideoRequest` field `plate_prompt`** -- the engine has\r\n  330: no ledger, `sampler_inputs_for(request)` is pure over the request, and `observability` is\r\n  331: never conditioning (`eng_ghost_signal_official.py:144-149`); this is the schema design item\r\n  332: that file names, taken deliberately.\r\n  333: \r\n  334: **D4 (mode routing) -- DROPPED: one subject-free scene plate per beat, plan untouched.**\r\n  335: `mode` is planned by ShotLock and reused on replay; an engine-side override would make the\r\n  336: rendered prompt differ from the planned row and break the same-prompt A/B. The plate carries\r\n  337: WORLD and MEDIUM only; the figure keeps coming from motif + leaf + law exactly as today\r\n  338: (`ghost_signal_prompt.py:863-867`), so Antigravity's \"random face per beat\" cannot occur --\r\n  339: there is no face in the plate. Figure plates are knob two. GO_FORWARD_PLAN 1.14's \"cycle\r\n  340: frozen to figure\" is corrected to this in the same change.\r\n  341: \r\n  342: **D5 (E1 mechanics) -- latent-direct, stock only, zero new node classes.** STAGE 2 encodes\r\n  343: the plate prompt as a third CLIPTextEncode before the CLIP is released. STAGE 3a (a bounded\r\n  344: `run_graph`): `plate_latent = EmptyLatentImage{512x288, 1}` -> `plate_sampler = KSampler{model:\r\n  345: Wire('base_model'), seed: request_seed, steps 20, cfg 8.0, euler, normal, denoise 1.0,\r\n  346: plate_cond, negative_cond}` -> the LATENT object returned in-process. Python:\r\n  347: `init = samples.repeat(U, 1, 1, 1)` with `RepeatLatentBatch`'s `batch_index` rule\r\n  348: (`ComfyUI/nodes.py:1314-1330`), U = `source_request`; no cap, fixed topology. STAGE 3b: the\r\n  349: shipping sampler graph with `latent_image` = the repeated latent as an `external_results`\r\n  350: entry and `denoise = E1_DENOISE`. STAGE 4: decode the beat as today; decode the PLATE once,\r\n  351: off the critical path, for the PNG. No `VAEEncode`, no `RepeatLatentBatch`, no\r\n  352: `VHS_DuplicateLatents` (installed, unprovisioned), no `ADE_UpscaleAndVAEEncode`. The seven-class\r\n  353: object_info capture stands; the peer gets its own instance-count pin (the haunted lane pins 8,\r\n  354: `tests/test_ghost_signal_haunted.py:165-170`).\r\n  355: \r\n  356: **D6 (seed) -- the plate uses `request_seed` itself.** Nothing new on the request; the plate is\r\n  357: a pure function of (checkpoint, plate prompt, seed, canvas, plate steps/cfg/sampler).\r\n  358: \r\n  359: **D7 (record and reuse).** The plate PNG is written to\r\n  360: `<episode>/stills/ghost_plates/<shot_id>_<sha8 of plate INPUTS>.png`; the replay bundle\r\n  361: already freezes `stills/` whole, so a replay REUSES a present sha-named plate (encoding it\r\n  362: instead of re-sampling) and the A/A is exact rather than exact-up-to-GPU-noise. Never a\r\n  363: fabricated dispatcher `images[]` row (those carry `content_hash` / `pool_path` / `provenance`\r\n  364: and node 91 verifies them). Verify at build that node 91 tolerates the unlisted file.\r\n  365: \r\n  366: **D8 (receipt) -- inputs only in the causal hash.** `sampler_inputs_for` returns the parent's\r\n  367: dict with `latent: 'ghost_plate_init'`, `init_image: None` (kept -- `accepts_still` is False),\r\n  368: `denoise: E1_DENOISE` (overriding the parent key), `plate_prompt` (full text), `plate_seed`,\r\n  369: `plate_steps / cfg / sampler / scheduler`, `plate_adapter_strength: 0.0`, `plate_canvas`,\r\n  370: `init_repeat_method: 'torch_repeat'`, `init_repeat_count: U`. NEVER the plate's rendered\r\n  371: sha, a path, a timestamp or minted/reused -- an OUTPUT in the causal hash makes the A/A false\r\n  372: by construction the first time SD1.5 is not bit-stable. `plate_sha256` rides beside the hash\r\n  373: like `vram_peak_mb` and in `CanonicalClip.qc` (`schemas.py:244`); no schema key on the clip.\r\n  374: `shot_cache_identity` gains plate-inputs sha8 + denoise. `E1_DENOISE` is a class attribute\r\n  375: with an env override read inside a method through the guarded parser (like `lora_strength`,\r\n  376: `eng_ghost_signal_official.py:158-174`), stamped on the receipt.\r\n  377: \r\n  378: **D9 (the proof) -- the 08-30 probe, run through the canonical graph.**\r\n  379: 1. G8 solo smoke (one beat): canvas probed, frame count exact, silence probed, VRAM peak\r\n  380:    receipted; split STAGE 3a/3b further if the peak exceeds 14.0 GB (Antigravity S2).\r\n  381: 2. Per style (anime, storybook_engraving, paper_origami): one canonical episode rendered on the\r\n  382:    lab profile at denoise 0.65 becomes the frozen source; replays: peer x2 at 0.65 (its OWN\r\n  383:    null -- the plate adds sampler noise), peer x1 each at 0.35 / 0.50 / 0.80, and the SAME\r\n  384:    bundle rendered on the SHIPPING lane via the replay engine override (D11) as the baseline.\r\n  385:    Every leg publishes to `otr/obs/`, clean runner, no harness title; `otr_verify_replay.py`\r\n  386:    on every pair.\r\n  387: 3. Measurement beside the eye: per-beat mean inter-frame difference (motion energy) for\r\n  388:    baseline, each denoise and both nulls, printed with a triptych card (plate | baseline frame\r\n  389:    0 | peer frame 0). E1 helped only if the operator's blinded style call rises while motion\r\n  390:    energy stays inside the null band; below the band is damping.\r\n  391: 4. Stop rules, in order: the plate PNGs do not read as the style (SD1.5 base with the full pack\r\n  392:    language is E1's ceiling; the next arm is E11, per-style checkpoints); no denoise both\r\n  393:    moves and keeps the plate (the 08-30 disqualification; go to the E2 probe); peak over\r\n  394:    14.5 GB (a 64x36 plate cannot do that; it would mean a patcher held twice).\r\n  395: \r\n  396: **D10 (not in this item) -- unchanged**, plus: no figure plates, no E1b, no ADE upgrade, no\r\n  397: Advanced-ControlNet.\r\n  398: \r\n  399: **D11 (NEW, on the instrument): a replay-time engine override.** The reused plan's shot rows\r\n  400: carry `engine_id`, so a replay renders on the FROZEN engine and a same-ledger cross-engine A/B\r\n  401: is impossible today. `otr_canonical_api_run.py --replay-engine <id>` (plus the writer's\r\n  402: `replay_from` path) re-stamps `engine_id` on every reused shot row for the roles the\r\n  403: override names, records `meta.replay_engine_override`, and leaves prompts, seeds, beats and\r\n  404: the frozen audio untouched. Default (no flag) stays the pure A/A. r2 designs where the\r\n  405: re-stamp lives (ShotLock's replay reuse branch is the natural seat) and how ShotLock's\r\n  406: per-engine prompt policy is re-applied without re-authoring.\r\n  407: \r\n  408: ## 8. What r2 (coding plan, Codex) must settle\r\n  409: \r\n  410: * The `VideoRequest.plate_prompt` field: optional str, default \"\", composed only for engines\r\n  411:   that declare `wants_plate_prompt = True`; where in `render_driver`'s Ghost branch; the\r\n  412:   budget test's fixture set.\r\n  413: * STAGE 3a/3b split: `run_graph` return shape for the LATENT, the `batch_index` rule, patcher\r\n  414:   ownership across the two calls (the base MODEL patcher is registered in `prepare`; the plate\r\n  415:   sampler must not detach it).\r\n  416: * D11's seat and its receipt; whether the override is per role or whole-plan.\r\n  417: * The instance-count pin and the `_node_candidates` map (no new classes; the map is the\r\n  418:   parent's).\r\n  419: * Tests: plate-prompt budget over ten packs; plate-prompt word bans (no name / camera /\r\n  420:   lettering / damping word); `sampler_inputs` pins; cache identity moves with plate inputs;\r\n  421:   receipts test \"plate inputs change the sha, plate output does not\".\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
