es\\schemas.py:168:    #: made every built request schema-invalid.\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:169:    observability: dict = Field(default_factory=dict)\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:170:\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:171:    @model_validator(mode=\"after\")\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:172:    def _check_family_required_inputs(self) -> \"VideoRequest\":\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:208:# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:209:# Output + plan models\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:210:# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:211:\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:212:\r\n> nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:213:class CanonicalClip(_Forbid):\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:214:    \"\"\"A normalized, ALWAYS-SILENT clip (or still/directory handoff).\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:215:\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:216:    Integer ``frame_count`` is the timing authority; color fields are \r\nrecorded\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:217:    and ffprobe-asserted (normalized to bt709 / yuv420p); ``alpha`` is \r\nexplicit\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:218:    and validated. ``has_audio`` is always False -- only \r\n``OTR_MasterAudioMux``\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:239:    engine_id: str = \"\"\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:240:    profile_id: str = \"\"\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:241:    family: str = \"\"\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:242:    request_hash: str = \"\"\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:243:    asset_hashes: list[str] = Field(default_factory=list)\r\n> nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:244:    qc: dict = Field(default_factory=dict)\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:245:    #: THE HONESTY RECEIPTS (no-mirror enforcement, 2026-08-06). How many of\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:246:    #: this clip's frames the engine actually RENDERED, and how the rest got\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:247:    #: there. ``native_frame_count`` is always the EMITTED count -- what the\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:248:    #: adapter handed back -- never a pre-trim decoded length, so it can \r\nnever\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:249:    #: exceed ``frame_count``. ``extension_mode`` is drawn from\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:250:    #: ``acceptance.EXTENSION_MODES``; ``\"none\"`` means every delivered \r\nframe was\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:251:    #: rendered, and it is the only mode that may ship.\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:252:    #:\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:253:    #: DECLARED HERE EVEN THOUGH THE RENDER PATH PASSES PLAIN DICTS. This \r\nclass\r\n> nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:254:    #: is ``extra=\"forbid\"``, so the day anything validates an adapter's \r\nreturn\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:255:    #: through it, an enriched clip carrying these two keys would be \r\nREJECTED as\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:256:    #: unknown fields -- the receipts would be dropped by the schema that \r\nexists\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:257:    #: to protect them. Adding them costs nothing today and removes a trap \r\nthat\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:258:    #: would otherwise fire far from its cause.\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:259:    native_frame_count: Optional[int] = None\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:260:    extension_mode: Optional[str] = None\r\n  nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:261:    #: THE CADENCE AND DELIVERY RECEIPTS (Ghost Signal, 2026-08-22). Declared\r\n> nodes\\_otr_video_engines\\schemas.py:262:    #: here for the same reason the 