stores the match exactly (probed), if it is\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:4069:- instrument note: `scripts/otr_replay_foley_mix.py` measures the mix, and its\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:4348:  produced this cast and can replay it -- and a lane-owned cast has no\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:4349:  `num_characters_request` to replay with. Claiming it detonated CastLock's\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:4350:  replay in a prior bug (`num_characters must be 1-6, got 0`).\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:4356:  `lock_cast()` is exactly what the writer's comment warns detonates the replay.\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:4371:  whose false claim caused the earlier replay detonation.\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:5666:  agy: fall back to the deterministic template) and BOTH were overruled at r4,\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:5702:  CastLock's replay (`num_characters must be 1-6, got 0`). The repair belongs in\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:6071:  template handling -- a plain `SD1Tokenizer` -- so the caller must supply it.\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:6073:  `llama_template=None` means \"use the built-in instruction template\", so plain\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:6207:## PBUG-20260823-01 -- the canonical runner's preflight model gate could never pass nine profiles\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:6232:## PBUG-20260823-02 -- the canonical runner reported a healthy render as RESULT TIMEOUT\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:7442:  fault. The replay instrument used to report both directions as \"NOT audible\";\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:7445:- verify idea: `scripts/otr_replay_foley_mix.py <episode_dir>` replays the mix\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:7447:  window) landing in the intended band; extend the replay to print that column\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:7578:- verify: the guard replayed over every joint-AV beat ever rendered flags\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:7677:  every haunted AnimateDiff beat (v3 + sliding context window, ~9-10 s/step at\r\ndocs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:7745:## PBUG-20260829-03 -- ComfyUI DynamicVRAM (`comfy_aimdo`) ABORTS THE PROCESS on an 8 GB OOM instead of ra