{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_98","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$p='\"'kibitz-runs/2026-09-02-still-in-peer/r2/input.md'; \"'$lines=Get-Content -LiteralPath $p; for($i=280;$i -le 421;$i++){ '\"'{0}:{1}' -f \"'$i,$lines[$i-1] }'","aggregated_output":"280:   suppress the trajectory while high-frequency texture boils. So Route A is a PROBE, not a\r\n281:   build: denoise 0.35 / 0.50 / 0.65 / 0.80, disqualified if <= 0.50 shows no macro-motion with\r\n282:   texture boil, or >= 0.65 loses the still within 2-3 frames. The mechanism is the same\r\n283:   whichever still is fed, which makes the still SOURCE a secondary question for the probe.\r\n284:2. **Upstream recommends the animated image come from the SAME SD1.5 model used for\r\n285:   animation**; a Z-Image still into a haunted SD1.5 checkpoint invites cross-model drift\r\n286:   (spec 11.5). This is the in-family plate's strongest reason, and it replaces the 4060\r\n287:   reasoning the anchor gave.\r\n288:\r\n289:The 08-30 spec's own recommendation (\"measure the image phase on the 4060 first, qualify\r\n290:Advanced-ControlNet, build SparseCtrl\") is superseded by the 09-02 campaign order, which\r\n291:deferred SparseCtrl (E7: a new pack pin, 1.99 GB, 323 MB of overnight headroom) and put the\r\n292:still-in probe here. Its Route A probe grid and disqualification rule are adopted verbatim.\r\n293:CLAUDE.md 0A forbids a standalone stock-node probe graph, so the probe VEHICLE is the lab\r\n294:peer itself rendering canonical episodes with a denoise knob, published to `otr/obs/`.\r\n295:\r\n296:## 7. Revised decisions after r1 (what r2 plans the code for)\r\n297:\r\n298:**D1 (id, receipt, lab status) -- unchanged.** `animatediff15_v3_stillin_lab_video`,\r\n299:recipe `animatediff_sd15_v3_haunted_stillin_e1_512x288_lab_v1`, `status: lab`, 5080 only,\r\n300:never a default, never a tombstoned id (`public_engines.py:398-402`).\r\n301:\r\n302:**D2 (in-family plate) -- STANDS, reasoning replaced.** The plate is minted in-graph from the\r\n303:same checkpoint because (a) upstream says the animated image should come from the animating\r\n304:model, (b) it needs no image phase (on 8 GB the image role is a native abort,\r\n305:PBUG-20260829-03; on the 5080 it is a cost the probe does not need to pay), and (c) it is the\r\n306:cheapest vehicle for the Route A probe, whose outcome is the same for either still source.\r\n307:`accepts_still` stays `False`, `required_inputs` `('text_prompt',)`, `still_plan` `()`,\r\n308:`subject_ownership` `'prompt'`, `prompt_profile` stays `GHOST_PROMPT_PROFILE` (or ShotLock\r\n309:stamps no `ghost_prompt` and render falls to v1, `otr_shot_lock.py:2137, 2246-2247`); the id\r\n310:joins `_ANIMATEDIFF_ENGINES` (`otr_provision.py:1516-1522`) so it stays in the no-still set.\r\n311:**E1b (dispatcher still, `accepts_still=True`, the 08-30 spec's contract corrected to\r\n312:`required_inputs=('text_prompt','init_image')` and a truthful non-empty `still_plan`) is the\r\n313:SECOND engine id, opened only if Route A survives the probe.**\r\n314:\r\n315:**D3 (plate prompt) -- replaced by the plate-prompt composer, modelled on\r\n316:`_compose_background_plate_prompt` (`otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1839-1865`).** Protected\r\n317:head, in order: the FULL `positive_tail` (never `compact_style_cue` / `prefix_style_cue`,\r\n318:`_otr_visual_styles.py:632-685` -- that IS the defect), `plate_look`, `_read_setting` top-2\r\n319:(`:40-49`), `get_era_tail(profile=\"still\")` (`_otr_story_brief_helpers.py:321-341`, capped\r\n320:120 chars). Droppable in fixed order: `era_tail`, `image_grade_tail`, atmosphere terms, the\r\n321:second setting term. NEVER: `scene_instruction_look` (an instruction sentence),\r\n322:`broadcast_tail`, any `motion_registers` entry (camera words; storybook's carry \"gently\" --\r\n323:a damping word), `open_subjects` / `announcer_*` / `portrait_*` (subject, identity), the leaf,\r\n324:the mode law, `NO_TEXT_CLAUSE`. Negative: the request's own composed Ghost negative\r\n325:(`ghost_signal_prompt.py:622-651`), verbatim. Budget: COUNTED with `measure_clip_tokens`\r\n326:(`ghost_signal_author.py:1234-1249`), `GhostBudgetError` if the protected head exceeds 69,\r\n327:pinned by a test over all nine packs plus a synthetic long `visual_storybased`. **The\r\n328:composition lives in `render_driver`'s Ghost branch (where `_vstyle` and ledger meta exist,\r\n329:`:2881-2950`) as a declared optional `VideoRequest` field `plate_prompt`** -- the engine has\r\n330:no ledger, `sampler_inputs_for(request)` is pure over the request, and `observability` is\r\n331:never conditioning (`eng_ghost_signal_official.py:144-149`); this is the schema design item\r\n332:that file names, taken deliberately.\r\n333:\r\n334:**D4 (mode routing) -- DROPPED: one subject-free scene plate per beat, plan untouched.**\r\n335:`mode` is planned by ShotLock and reused on replay; an engine-side override would make the\r\n336:rendered prompt differ from the planned row and break the same-prompt A/B. The plate carries\r\n337:WORLD and MEDIUM only; the figure keeps coming from motif + leaf + law exactly as today\r\n338:(`ghost_signal_prompt.py:863-867`), so Antigravity's \"random face per beat\" cannot occur --\r\n339:there is no face in the plate. Figure plates are knob two. GO_FORWARD_PLAN 1.14's \"cycle\r\n340:frozen to figure\" is corrected to this in the same change.\r\n341:\r\n342:**D5 (E1 mechanics) -- latent-direct, stock only, zero new node classes.** STAGE 2 encodes\r\n343:the plate prompt as a third CLIPTextEncode before the CLIP is released. STAGE 3a (a bounded\r\n344:`run_graph`): `plate_latent = EmptyLatentImage{512x288, 1}` -> `plate_sampler = KSampler{model:\r\n345:Wire('base_model'), seed: request_seed, steps 20, cfg 8.0, euler, normal, denoise 1.0,\r\n346:plate_cond, negative_cond}` -> the LATENT object returned in-process. Python:\r\n347:`init = samples.repeat(U, 1, 1, 1)` with `RepeatLatentBatch`'s `batch_index` rule\r\n348:(`ComfyUI/nodes.py:1314-1330`), U = `source_request`; no cap, fixed topology. STAGE 3b: the\r\n349:shipping sampler graph with `latent_image` = the repeated latent as an `external_results`\r\n350:entry and `denoise = E1_DENOISE`. STAGE 4: decode the beat as today; decode the PLATE once,\r\n351:off the critical path, for the PNG. No `VAEEncode`, no `RepeatLatentBatch`, no\r\n352:`VHS_DuplicateLatents` (installed, unprovisioned), no `ADE_UpscaleAndVAEEncode`. The seven-class\r\n353:object_info capture stands; the peer gets its own instance-count pin (the haunted lane pins 8,\r\n354:`tests/test_ghost_signal_haunted.py:165-170`).\r\n355:\r\n356:**D6 (seed) -- the plate uses `request_seed` itself.** Nothing new on the request; the plate is\r\n357:a pure function of (checkpoint, plate prompt, seed, canvas, plate steps/cfg/sampler).\r\n358:\r\n359:**D7 (record and reuse).** The plate PNG is written to\r\n360:`<episode>/stills/ghost_plates/<shot_id>_<sha8 of plate INPUTS>.png`; the replay bundle\r\n361:already freezes `stills/` whole, so a replay REUSES a present sha-named plate (encoding it\r\n362:instead of re-sampling) and the A/A is exact rather than exact-up-to-GPU-noise. Never a\r\n363:fabricated dispatcher `images[]` row (those carry `content_hash` / `pool_path` / `provenance`\r\n364:and node 91 verifies them). Verify at build that node 91 tolerates the unlisted file.\r\n365:\r\n366:**D8 (receipt) -- inputs only in the causal hash.** `sampler_inputs_for` returns the parent's\r\n367:dict with `latent: 'ghost_plate_init'`, `init_image: None` (kept -- `accepts_still` is False),\r\n368:`denoise: E1_DENOISE` (overriding the parent key), `plate_prompt` (full text), `plate_seed`,\r\n369:`plate_steps / cfg / sampler / scheduler`, `plate_adapter_strength: 0.0`, `plate_canvas`,\r\n370:`init_repeat_method: 'torch_repeat'`, `init_repeat_count: U`. NEVER the plate's rendered\r\n371:sha, a path, a timestamp or minted/reused -- an OUTPUT in the causal hash makes the A/A false\r\n372:by construction the first time SD1.5 is not bit-stable. `plate_sha256` rides beside the hash\r\n373:like `vram_peak_mb` and in `CanonicalClip.qc` (`schemas.py:244`); no schema key on the clip.\r\n374:`shot_cache_identity` gains plate-inputs sha8 + denoise. `E1_DENOISE` is a class attribute\r\n375:with an env override read inside a method through the guarded parser (like `lora_strength`,\r\n376:`eng_ghost_signal_official.py:158-174`), stamped on the receipt.\r\n377:\r\n378:**D9 (the proof) -- the 08-30 probe, run through the canonical graph.**\r\n379:1. G8 solo smoke (one beat): canvas probed, frame count exact, silence probed, VRAM peak\r\n380:   receipted; split STAGE 3a/3b further if the peak exceeds 14.0 GB (Antigravity S2).\r\n381:2. Per style (anime, storybook_engraving, paper_origami): one canonical episode rendered on the\r\n382:   lab profile at denoise 0.65 becomes the frozen source; replays: peer x2 at 0.65 (its OWN\r\n383:   null -- the plate adds sampler noise), peer x1 each at 0.35 / 0.50 / 0.80, and the SAME\r\n384:   bundle rendered on the SHIPPING lane via the replay engine override (D11) as the baseline.\r\n385:   Every leg publishes to `otr/obs/`, clean runner, no harness title; `otr_verify_replay.py`\r\n386:   on every pair.\r\n387:3. Measurement beside the eye: per-beat mean inter-frame difference (motion energy) for\r\n388:   baseline, each denoise and both nulls, printed with a triptych card (plate | baseline frame\r\n389:   0 | peer frame 0). E1 helped only if the operator's blinded style call rises while motion\r\n390:   energy stays inside the null band; below the band is damping.\r\n391:4. Stop rules, in order: the plate PNGs do not read as the style (SD1.5 base with the full pack\r\n392:   language is E1's ceiling; the next arm is E11, per-style checkpoints); no denoise both\r\n393:   moves and keeps the plate (the 08-30 disqualification; go to the E2 probe); peak over\r\n394:   14.5 GB (a 64x36 plate cannot do that; it would mean a patcher held twice).\r\n395:\r\n396:**D10 (not in this item) -- unchanged**, plus: no figure plates, no E1b, no ADE upgrade, no\r\n397:Advanced-ControlNet.\r\n398:\r\n399:**D11 (NEW, on the instrument): a replay-time engine override.** The reused plan's shot rows\r\n400:carry `engine_id`, so a replay renders on the FROZEN engine and a same-ledger cross-engine A/B\r\n401:is impossible today. `otr_canonical_api_run.py --replay-engine <id>` (plus the writer's\r\n402:`replay_from` path) re-stamps `engine_id` on every reused shot row for the roles the\r\n403:override names, records `meta.replay_engine_override`, and leaves prompts, seeds, beats and\r\n404:the frozen audio untouched. Default (no flag) stays the pure A/A. r2 designs where the\r\n405:re-stamp lives (ShotLock's replay reuse branch is the natural seat) and how ShotLock's\r\n406:per-engine prompt policy is re-applied without re-authoring.\r\n407:\r\n408:## 8. What r2 (coding plan, Codex) must settle\r\n409:\r\n410:* The `VideoRequest.plate_prompt` field: optional str, default \"\", composed only for engines\r\n411:  that declare `wants_plate_prompt = True`; where in `render_driver`'s Ghost branch; the\r\n412:  budget test's fixture set.\r\n413:* STAGE 3a/3b split: `run_graph` return shape for the LATENT, the `batch_index` rule, patcher\r\n414:  ownership across the two calls (the base MODEL patcher is registered in `prepare`; the plate\r\n415:  sampler must not detach it).\r\n416:* D11's seat and its receipt; whether the override is per role or whole-plan.\r\n417:* The instance-count pin and the `_node_candidates` map (no new classes; the map is the\r\n418:  parent's).\r\n419:* Tests: plate-prompt budget over ten packs; plate-prompt word bans (no name / camera /\r\n420:  lettering / damping word); `sampler_inputs` pins; cache identity moves with plate inputs;\r\n421:  receipts test \"plate inputs change the sha, pla