is ledger never passed through the OTR_VideoDirector /\r\n5152:    OTR_ShotLock freeze: a legacy fixture, or one of the two shipped HTTP entry\r\n5153:    points (``/otr/video_render_single``, ``/otr/video_render_soak``) that build\r\n5154:    a ledger by hand with no OTR_VideoDirector upstream. Those keep the historic\r\n5155:    mutating behaviour -- see :func:`resolve_final_shot_engines`.\r\n5156:    \"\"\"\r\n5157:    section = (ledger or {}).get(\"video\") or {}\r\n5158:    frozen = section.get(\"roles_effective\")\r\n5159:    return dict(frozen) if isinstance(frozen, dict) and frozen else {}\r\n5160:\r\n5161:\r\n5162:def assert_frozen_route(ledger):\r\n5163:    \"\"\"VERIFY the frozen route instead of re-deriving it. Returns True if a\r\n5164:    frozen route was present (and therefore verified), False if there is none.\r\n5165:\r\n5166:    Never mutates. Raises :class:`RenderError` on ANY disagreement:\r\n5167:\r\n5168:    * the routing ENVIRONMENT moved since the freeze, so the frozen map no\r\n5169:      longer describes what will render;\r\n5170:    * a shot's engine/family is not what the freeze said it would be;\r\n5171:    * a shot disagrees with its own execution group.\r\n5172:\r\n5173:    WHY AN ASSERTION AND NOT A REPAIR (2026-07-25, chunk 1c). Repairing here is\r\n5174:    what the old code did, and it is why the defect survived so long: the\r\n5175:    render phase silently corrected a route the image phase had already planned\r\n5176:    stills for, so the two phases disagreed and only the pixels showed it. If\r\n5177:    the plan and the environment disagree at render time, the stills are\r\n5178:    already wrong and no mutation of the shot rows can un-mint them. Fail loud,\r\n5179:    before GPU time.\r\n5180:    \"\"\"\r\n5181:    frozen = frozen_route_from_ledger(ledger)\r\n5182:    if not frozen:\r\n5183:        return False\r\n5184:\r\n5185:    section = (ledger or {}).get(\"video\") or {}\r\n5186:    try:\r\n5187:        from .._otr_shared import route_freeze as _rf  # type: ignore\r\n5188:    except ImportError:  # pragma: no cover -- flat test imports\r\n5189:        from _otr_shared import route_freeze as _rf  # type: ignore\r\n5190:\r\n5191:    stamped_env = section.get(\"routing_env_snapshot\")\r\n5192:    if isinstance(stamped_env, dict) and stamped_env:\r\n5193:        live_env = _rf.routing_env_snapshot()\r\n5194:        if not _rf.snapshots_agree(stamped_env, live_env):\r\n5195:            raise RenderError(\r\n5196:                \"ROUTE EQUALITY: the routing environment changed after the \"\r\n5197:                \"plan was frozen (frozen %r, live %r). Every still and prompt \"\r\n5198:                \"in this episode was planned for the frozen route, so \"\r\n5199:                \"rendering the live one would render engines the image phase \"\r\n5200:                \"never minted assets for. Re-run from OTR_VideoDirector. \"\r\n5201:                \"NO FALLBACK.\" % (stamped_env, live_env))\r\n5202:\r\n5203:    groups_by_id = {}\r\n5204:    for grp in section.get(\"execution_groups\") or ():\r\n5205:        if isinstance(grp, dict):\r\n5206:            groups_by_id[str(grp.get(\"group_id\") or \"\")] = str(\r\n5207:                grp.get(\"engine_id\") or \"\")\r\n5208:\r\n5209:    for shot in section.get(\"shots\") or ():\r\n5210:        if not isinstance(shot, dict):\r\n5211:            continue\r\n5212:        role = str(shot.get(\"role\") or _role_of_shot(shot) or \"\")\r\n5213:        expected = str(frozen.get(role) or \"\")\r\n5214:        actual = str(shot.get(\"engine_id\") or \"\")\r\n5215:        if not expected:\r\n5216:            # A shot whose role the freeze never covered (2026-07-25 QA). The\r\n5217:            # docstring promises to catch ANY disagreement, and silently\r\n5218:            # skipping an unmapped role is the one hole that promise had: the\r\n5219:            # shot would render on whatever engine its row happens to carry,\r\n5220:            # unve