y distorted on the way to 1920x1080. Asserting it HERE, at the\r\n1097:        seam where the mode is stamped, is what makes that safe.\r\n1098:        \"\"\"\r\n1099:        raw = raw or {}\r\n1100:        path = raw.get(\"out_path\", \"\")\r\n1101:        if path:\r\n1102:            fields = ffprobe_clip_fields(path)\r\n1103:            validate_silent_clip_contract(fields, self.target_fps)\r\n1104:            width = int(fields.get(\"width\") or 0)\r\n1105:            height = int(fields.get(\"height\") or 0)\r\n1106:            if width != GHOST_CANVAS_W or height != GHOST_CANVAS_H:\r\n1107:                raise RuntimeError(\r\n1108:                    \"%s produced a %dx%d clip; this lane delivers by clean \"\r\n1109:                    \"full-frame Lanczos with no pad or crop, so only an exact \"\r\n1110:                    \"%dx%d source can be enlarged to %dx%d without distorting \"\r\n1111:                    \"it\" % (self.name, width, height, GHOST_CANVAS_W,\r\n1112:                            GHOST_CANVAS_H, GHOST_DELIVERY_W, GHOST_DELIVERY_H))\r\n1113:\r\n1114:        clip = self._clip_from_raw(raw, request)\r\n1115:        for key in (\"model_frame_count\", \"cadence_mode\",\r\n1116:                    \"cadence_source_frame_count\",\r\n1117:                    \"cadence_delivered_frame_count\", \"cadence_tail_trim\",\r\n1118:                    \"delivery_scale_mode\"):\r\n1119:            if key in raw:\r\n1120:                clip[key] = raw[key]\r\n1121:        return clip\r\n1122:\r\n1123:    def _clip_from_raw(self, raw, request):\r\n120:class GhostSignalV3HauntedEngine(GhostSignalV3Engine):\r\n121:    \"\"\"``animatediff15_v3_haunted_video`` -- v3 plus the removable adapter.\r\n122:\r\n123:    A THIRD peer, additive exactly as v3 and v2 were. It inherits everything\r\n124:    from the clean v3 lane and adds one thing: the domain adapter on the MODEL\r\n125:    path. The clean v3 lane sits beside it as the reference and the golden lane\r\n126:    is untouched, so a comparison between them is a one-variable comparison.\r\n127:\r\n128:    WHY THE ADAPTER IS INTERESTING HERE. Ghost's worst tendency is lettering --\r\n129:    SD1.5 volunteers text into anything resembling a sign, a poster or a radio\r\n130:    dial, which is most of this show, and the lane fights that with\r\n131:    negative-prompt tokens on every single beat. The adapter is a different\r\n132:    mechanism aimed at the same class of defect: rather than arguing with the\r\n133:    model at inference, upstream parks the training set's learned artifacts in\r\n134:    a removable component. Turned DOWN it should mean less learned grime;\r\n135:    turned UP, more of it, deliberately, as a look.\r\n136:\r\n137:    IT LOADS ON THE STOCK NODE. The artifact carries 256 UNet attention tensors\r\n138:    and ZERO text-encoder tensors -- read off the checkpoint's own key list,\r\n139:    not its documentation -- which is why this is ``LoraLoaderModelOnly`` and\r\n140:    why CLIP keeps its untouched path. The keys are the legacy diffusers\r\n141:    attn-processor spelling, which ComfyUI maps natively, so there is no\r\n142:    conversion step and no custom loader anywhere in this lane.\r\n143:\r\n144:    WHAT IS NOT HERE YET: nothing schedules the strength across an episode. The\r\n145:    dial is one frozen number per render. Driving it from the ledger's arc so\r\n146:    the picture degrades as the story tightens needs a declared field on\r\n147:    ``VideoRequest`` -- that model is ``extra=\"forbid\"`` and its one open dict\r\n148:    is documented \"NEVER conditioning\" -- and a schema change is a design item,\r\n149:    not a mechanical one. Prove the dial does something first.\r\n150:    \"\"\"\r\n151:\r\n152:    name = \"animatediff15_v3_haunted_video\"\r\n153:\r\n154:    lora_name = ADAPTER_V3_NAME\r\n155:    lora_min_bytes = ADAPTER_V3_MIN_BYTES\r\n156:    recipe_receipt_id = \"animatediff_sd15_v3_haunted_static16_512x288_v1\"\r\n157:\r\n158:    @property\r\n159:    def lora_strength(self):\r\n160:        \"\"\"Frozen default, overridable for the strength sweep.\r\n161:\r\n162:        A property rather than a plain constant because the point of the first\r\n163:        renders is to try several values without editing code between them.\r\n164:        An unreadable or absent value lands on the frozen default rather than\r\n165:        on zero: zero would render the CLEAN lane while stamping a haunted\r\n166:        receipt, which is the one outcome this lane may never produce.\r\n167:        \"\"\"\r\n168:        raw = os.environ.get(ADAPTER_V3_STRENGTH_ENV)\r\n169:        if raw is None or not str(raw).strip():\r\n170:            return ADAPTER_V3_STRENGTH\r\n171:        try:\r\n172:            return float(raw)\r\n173:        except (TypeError, ValueError):\r\n174:            return ADAPTER_V3_STRENGTH\r\n175:\r\n176:\r\n177:__all__ = [\"GhostSignalV3Engine\",\r\n178:           \"GhostSignalV3HauntedEngine\",\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
