{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_113","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$p='\"'nodes/production_ledger.py'; \"'$l=Get-Content -LiteralPath $p; for($i=624;$i -le 720;$i++){'\"'{0}:{1}' -f \"'$i,$l[$i-1]}; $p='\"'scripts/otr_freeze_replay_bundle.py'; \"'$l=Get-Content -LiteralPath $p; for($i=1;$i -le 30;$i++){'\"'{0}:{1}' -f \"'$i,$l[$i-1]}; for($i=130;$i -le 170;$i++){'\"'{0}:{1}' -f \"'$i,$l[$i-1]}'","aggregated_output":"624:def import_replay_bundle(bundle_dir: str, new_episode_id: Optional[str] = None) -> \"Ledger\":\r\n625:    \"\"\"ONE validated clone of a frozen episode into a NEW workspace, and the\r\n626:    process singleton rebound to it (campaign item 0, 2026-09-02).\r\n627:\r\n628:    What it does, in order: validate the manifest (schema, relative paths,\r\n629:    digests); deep-copy the bundle's ledger; give it the new root episode id\r\n630:    and remember the source under ``meta.replay_of_episode``; stamp\r\n631:    ``meta.replay_from`` and a workspace-unique ``meta.replay_workspace_id``\r\n632:    (the freeze receipt stays byte-identical); materialize the bundle's stills,\r\n633:    portraits and canon into the new episode dir; rebase every episode-local\r\n634:    path (``path`` AND ``pool_path``, and every other absolute pointer below\r\n635:    the old root) onto the new dir; re-file the publication receipt under the\r\n636:    new id; clear the source's terminal / obs pointers and its run-volatile\r\n637:    telemetry (render engines, render trace, phase timings); ``new_ledger``\r\n638:    so ``in_flight_ledger_path()`` binds the new workspace; save atomically.\r\n639:    The master WAV is NOT copied here: node 7 (EpisodeAssembler) owns that\r\n640:    file and copies it onto its canonical name, verified, before it emits\r\n641:    ``audio_done``.\"\"\"\r\n642:    bundle = os.path.abspath(bundle_dir)\r\n643:    manifest = load_replay_manifest(bundle)\r\n644:    source_id = str(manifest[\"source_episode_id\"])\r\n645:    new_id = str(new_episode_id or \"\").strip() or replay_episode_id(source_id)\r\n646:    ledger_path = os.path.join(bundle, *manifest[\"ledger\"].split(\"/\"))\r\n647:    with open(ledger_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\r\n648:        source = json.load(fh)\r\n649:    if not isinstance(source, dict) or not source.get(\"lines\"):\r\n650:        raise ReplayBundleError(\"bundle ledger carries no lines\")\r\n651:    data = copy.deepcopy(source)\r\n652:    meta = data.get(\"meta\")\r\n653:    if not isinstance(meta, dict):\r\n654:        meta = {}\r\n655:        data[\"meta\"] = meta\r\n656:    old_root = str(manifest.get(\"source_episode_root\") or \"\")\r\n657:\r\n658:    led = new_ledger(episode_id=new_id)          # binds _CURRENT + makes the dir\r\n659:    new_audio_dir = led.out_dir\r\n660:    new_root = os.path.dirname(new_audio_dir)\r\n661:    # materialize the bundle's assets under the new episode dir, by relative path\r\n662:    materialized = {}\r\n663:    for row in manifest[\"files\"]:\r\n664:        rel = _safe_relative(row[\"path\"])\r\n665:        if rel in (manifest[\"ledger\"], manifest[\"master_audio\"]):\r\n666:            continue\r\n667:        src = os.path.join(bundle, *rel.split(\"/\"))\r\n668:        dst = os.path.join(new_root, *rel.split(\"/\"))\r\n669:        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)\r\n670:        if os.path.abspath(src) != os.path.abspath(dst):\r\n671:            shutil.copyfile(src, dst)\r\n672:        materialized[rel] = dst\r\n673:    # identity + provenance\r\n674:    data[\"episode_id\"] = new_id\r\n675:    meta[\"episode_id\"] = new_id\r\n676:    meta[\"replay_of_episode\"] = source_id\r\n677:    meta[\"replay_from\"] = bundle\r\n678:    meta[\"replay_workspace_id\"] = uuid.uuid4().hex\r\n679:    meta[\"replay_source_commit\"] = str(manifest.get(\"source_commit\") or \"\")\r\n680:    meta[\"replay_master_audio\"] = manifest[\"master_audio\"]\r\n681:    meta[\"replay_master_sha256\"] = next(\r\n682:        (str(r.get(\"sha256\") or \"\") for r in manifest[\"files\"]\r\n683:         if _safe_relative(r.get(\"path\")) == manifest[\"master_audio\"]), \"\")\r\n684:    # the source's run-volatile telemetry and terminal pointers do not carry over\r\n685:    for key in _REPLAY_RUN_VOLATILE_META:\r\n686:        meta.pop(key, None)\r\n687:    for key in (\"final_audio_path\", \"final_video_path\"):\r\n688:        data[key] = None\r\n689:    for key in (\"obs_publish\", \"obs_path\", \"published_path\"):\r\n690:        meta.pop(key, None)\r\n691:    # rebase every episode-local absolute path onto the new root\r\n692:    if old_root:\r\n693:        data, _n = _rebase_episode_local_paths(data, old_root, new_root)\r\n694:    led.data = data\r\n695:    led._rebase_publication_eligibility(new_id)\r\n696:    path = led.save()\r\n697:    if path is None:\r\n698:        raise ReplayBundleError(\"import_replay_bundle: the imported ledger did not save\")\r\n699:    log.info(\"[Ledger] replay workspace %s imported from %s (source %s, %d asset(s))\",\r\n700:             new_id, bundle, source_id, len(materialized))\r\n701:    return led\r\n702:\r\n703:\r\n704:def peek_ledger() -> Optional[\"Ledger\"]:\r\n705:    \"\"\"Return the current ledger or None. Never creates a placeholder.\r\n706:\r\n707:    Use this from downstream nodes (reviewer, sequencer, audit\r\n708:    artifacts) where an absent ledger is an error condition rather\r\n709:    than a fresh-run signal.\r\n710:    \"\"\"\r\n711:    with _LEDGER_LOCK:\r\n712:        return _CURRENT\r\n713:\r\n714:\r\n715:class LedgerStampError(RuntimeError):\r\n716:    \"\"\"S2 durable-persistence contract (credits enrichment 2026-07-03):\r\n717:    a required credits stamp could not be persisted to the production\r\n718:    ledger singleton. LOUD by design -- the late OTR_CreditsRoll node can\r\n719:    only read what is on disk, so a silent save miss here becomes a\r\n720:    missing-receipt failure at mux time. Never catch-and-continue.\"\"\"\r\n1:\"\"\"Freeze a finished episode into a REPLAY BUNDLE (campaign item 0, 2026-09-02).\r\n2:\r\n3:    python scripts/otr_freeze_replay_bundle.py <episode dir or episode id> [--out DIR]\r\n4:\r\n5:The bundle is what the canonical graph replays: the writer's ``replay_from`` widget\r\n6:(or ``otr_canonical_api_run.py --replay-from``) points at it, the writer short-circuits\r\n7:authorship, the audio chain passes through, node 7 copies the frozen master, ShotLock\r\n8:reuses the PLANNED video section, node 91 verifies the imported stills, and only the\r\n9:video phase and the publish tail run -- the same seeds, the same audio, a new episode.\r\n10:\r\n11:WHAT IS FROZEN: the durable ledger, the master WAV, ``episode_canon.json``, every file\r\n12:under ``stills/`` and ``portraits/``. NOT frozen: clips, composites, the published MP4 --\r\n13:the replay makes its own. The manifest is a safe import format: relative paths only,\r\n14:sizes and SHA-256 per file, the source episode id, root and commit; built in a temporary\r\n15:sibling directory and renamed into place only after every file was verified. Freezing is\r\n16:explicit and operator-visible; nothing freezes itself.\r\n17:\r\n18:The ledger MUST carry the planned ``video.shots`` (stamped durably by ShotLock since\r\n19:2026-09-02) -- a replay without the plan would re-author prompts through the LLM, which is\r\n20:not a replay. Refused otherwise unless ``--allow-no-plan`` is passed for a diagnostic.\r\n21:\"\"\"\r\n22:from __future__ import annotations\r\n23:\r\n24:import argparse\r\n25:import hashlib\r\n26:import json\r\n27:import os\r\n28:import pathlib\r\n29:import shutil\r\n30:import subprocess\r\n130:\r\n131:    def _add(src: pathlib.Path, rel: str) -> None:\r\n132:        if not src.is_file() or src.stat().st_size <= 0:\r\n133:            raise SystemExit(\"refusing to freeze a missing or empty file: %s\" % src)\r\n134:        dst 