{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_119","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$p='\"'nodes/otr_shot_lock.py'; \"'$l=Get-Content -LiteralPath $p; for($i=1938;$i -le 2095;$i++){'\"'{0}:{1}' -f \"'$i,$l[$i-1]}'","aggregated_output":"1938:    shot[\"frame_bounded\"] = bool(_fc.can_split(engine))\r\n1939:\r\n1940:\r\n1941:def _stamp_coverage_plan(shot, beat_id, *, max_render_frames):\r\n1942:    \"\"\"Attach this beat's durable ``coverage_plan`` to its shot row (chunk 3b).\r\n1943:\r\n1944:    Resolves the shot's engine to its declared :class:`FrameContract` and\r\n1945:    partitions the beat's ``target_frame_count`` into legal render segments.\r\n1946:    Validated here, at the plan boundary, so a plan that cannot be executed\r\n1947:    never reaches the wire.\r\n1948:\r\n1949:    ``max_render_frames`` IS REQUIRED, keyword-only, and has no default (B3,\r\n1950:    2026-07-26). It is the tier's render-length ceiling off the same ``policy``\r\n1951:    dict the ledger stamp reads, and for the engines in\r\n1952:    ``frame_contract.PLANNING_CAP_ENGINES`` it NARROWS the contract this beat\r\n1953:    is partitioned against -- see :func:`frame_contract.effective_frame_contract`\r\n1954:    for why membership is a per-engine decision with a live proof attached\r\n1955:    rather than a rollout. (This read \"why that allowlist is one engine long\r\n1956:    and why WAN must stay out of it\"; both halves went stale. It is three\r\n1957:    engines, and ``wan_ti2v`` joined on 2026-08-02 when the no-mirror ruling\r\n1958:    removed the adapter-side ping-pong that had made its ceiling harmless.)\r\n1959:    A default of 0 was proposed and rejected: it would let a caller that forgot\r\n1960:    the ceiling plan silently unpinned, which is the exact silent-fallback\r\n1961:    shape this build exists to remove. There is one caller; it passes the\r\n1962:    value. When the ceiling narrows anything, the resulting contract is stamped\r\n1963:    beside the plan as ``shot[\"coverage_contract\"]`` and the render boundary\r\n1964:    re-derives it and requires exact equality.\r\n1965:\r\n1966:    FAIL-CLOSED ON A REAL PARTITION FAILURE, tolerant of an ABSENT one. A\r\n1967:    :class:`CoveragePlanError` means the adapter genuinely cannot cover this\r\n1968:    beat -- for a ``single_only`` engine that means the beat exceeds its cap,\r\n1969:    which today is answered by ping-pong, loop-fill or a held frame, i.e. the\r\n1970:    three silent mechanisms this build removes. That must surface, so it\r\n1971:    propagates. An engine that is simply not registered yet (a custom slot, a\r\n1972:    test stub) gets NO plan rather than a guessed one: the row stays absent and\r\n1973:    the render path behaves exactly as it did before 3b.\r\n1974:\r\n1975:    ALSO MINTS THE JUMP-STILL REQUESTS (2026-07-25, chunk 4). A jump segment is\r\n1976:    an independent render with nothing to begin from, so every segment after\r\n1977:    the first owes the image phase its own still. They are minted HERE, where\r\n1978:    ``beat_id`` is authoritative rather than re-derived, and stamped durably so\r\n1979:    the image dispatcher and the still spine can READ the ids.\r\n1980:\r\n1981:    ONLY FOR A LANE THAT ACTUALLY CONSUMES A STILL (2026-07-25 QA fix). The\r\n1982:    question is asked with ``render_driver._still_spine_requires_scene`` -- the\r\n1983:    SAME predicate the spine will use to demand the stills back. That identity\r\n1984:    is the point. Minting unconditionally created a contradiction with a real\r\n1985:    failure: for an audio-reactive visualizer beat (no scene object, no\r\n1986:    required target) the image dispatcher correctly concluded the lane needs no\r\n1987:    still and skipped, while the spine still demanded every stamped request and\r\n1988:    raised ``RenderError`` before the first render. Two policies over one state,\r\n1989:    whichever fires first wins -- the defect shape this build exists to remove.\r\n1990:    One predicate, asked at the mint, and the disagreement cannot be\r\n1991:    constructed.\r\n1992:    \"\"\"\r\n1993:    target = int(shot.get(\"target_frame_count\") or 0)\r\n1994:    if target < 1:\r\n1995:        return                      # a zero-length beat has nothing to cover\r\n1996:    engine_id = str(shot.get(\"engine_id\") or \"\")\r\n1997:    if not engine_id:\r\n1998:        return\r\n1999:    try:\r\n2000:        from ._otr_video_engines import registry as _vreg_local  # type: ignore\r\n2001:        from ._otr_video_engines import frame_contract as _fc  # type: ignore\r\n2002:        from ._otr_video_engines import coverage_plan as _cp  # type: ignore\r\n2003:    except ImportError:  # pragma: no cover -- flat test imports\r\n2004:        from _otr_video_engines import registry as _vreg_local  # type: ignore\r\n2005:        from _otr_video_engines import frame_contract as _fc  # type: ignore\r\n2006:        from _otr_video_engines import coverage_plan as _cp  # type: ignore\r\n2007:    if not _vreg_local.is_registered(engine_id):\r\n2008:        return\r\n2009:    try:\r\n2010:        declared = _fc.frame_contract_for(_vreg_local.get_engine(engine_id))\r\n2011:    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- an unbuildable engine gets no plan\r\n2012:        return\r\n2013:    # THE TIER CEILING PLANS (B3, 2026-07-26), and this call sits OUTSIDE the\r\n2014:    # except above ON PURPOSE. It raises PlanningCapError for a ceiling no\r\n2015:    # legal segment fits under, and that catch means \"unbuildable engine, give\r\n2016:    # it no plan\" -- absorbing a misconfigured ceiling into it would produce a\r\n2017:    # beat with NO coverage plan, indistinguishable in the log from an\r\n2018:    # unregistered engine, which is chunk 1a's swallowed-fail-closed shape.\r\n2019:    # Three independent reviewers named this line before it was written.\r\n2020:    #\r\n2021:    # ``declared`` STAYS BOUND to the static contract. Both derivations below\r\n2022:    # take the DECLARED one: feeding the already-narrowed contract back into\r\n2023:    # ``coverage_contract_receipt`` makes it compare equal to itself and return\r\n2024:    # None, so the receipt would silently never be stamped and the render\r\n2025:    # boundary would have nothing to check.\r\n2026:    contract = _fc.effective_frame_contract(engine_id, declared,\r\n2027:                                            max_render_frames)\r\n2028:    plan = _cp.partition_beat(target, contract)\r\n2029:    _cp.validate_coverage_plan(plan, contract)\r\n2030:\r\n2031:    # HISTORY -- THE REFUSAL THAT USED TO LIVE HERE, kept because the reasoning\r\n2032:    # is what makes the lift below safe to read. It was written 2026-07-26 by\r\n2033:    # the chunk 7a QA panel and REMOVED 2026-07-29 once its prerequisite was\r\n2034:    # built; the note after it says by what.\r\n2035:    #\r\n2036:    # A lane that REQUIRES an audio_ref generates its\r\n2037:    # frames FROM that audio -- HuMo animates a mouth against speech. Splitting\r\n2038:    # such a beat into segments needs each segment to receive its own slice of\r\n2039:    # that speech, and nothing in this build slices it: ``_voice_audio_for_line``\r\n2040:    # takes a line and returns one path, with no segment index anywhere in its\r\n2041:    # signature or its callers.\r\n2042:    #\r\n2043:    # So a split HuMo beat would hand EVERY segment the whole line from its\r\n2044:    # start, and the assembled clip would speak the opening syllables three\r\n2045:    # times over while the audio ran on. That is a sync defect that ships as a\r\n2046:    # finished episode -- the exact failure class this build exists to remove,\r\n2047:    # and worse than the refusal because nothing in the log would say so.\r\n2048:    #\r\n2049:    # Refusing here is not a new gate; it is the SAME refusal moved earlier and\r\n2050:    # given a reason. ``humo_14B_169`` already raised ``MirrorExtensionForbidden``\r\n2051:    # at render time for any beat past its 49-frame cap -- after the GPU work,\r\n2052:    # with a message about mirroring. This one lands at plan time, names the\r\n2053:    # beat, and says what is actually missing.\r\n2054:    # THE REFUSAL ABOVE IS LIFTED (WIRE-W4e, 2026-07-29) BECAUSE ITS STATED\r\n2055:    # PREREQUISITE NOW EXISTS. It read, in full:\r\n2056:    #\r\n2057:    #     \"beat %s needs %d clips on %s ... but %s renders frames FROM its\r\n2058:    #      audio_ref and nothing in this build slices that audio per segment\r\n2059:    #      -- every segment would receive the whole line from its start and\r\n2060:    #      the assembled beat would repeat the opening syllables. NO FALLBACK:\r\n2061:    #      per-segment audio is the prerequisite, not a workaround.\"\r\n2062:    #\r\n2063:    # It was right, and it was right to name the prerequisite instead of\r\n2064:    # inventing a workaround. That prerequisite is now built, for BOTH audio\r\n2065:    # sources a beat can have:\r\n2066:    #\r\n2067:    #   * the FROZEN MASTER slice -- WIRE-W4b narrowed it to the segment's own\r\n2068:    #     render window, and WIRE-W4c made the trimmed tail silence rather than\r\n2069:    #     the next beat's speech (r4/A4).\r\n2070:    #   * a PER-LINE VOICE WAV -- WIRE-W4e slices that too, from its own zero,\r\n2071:    #     through the same `coverage_plan.segment_render_window` authority.\r\n2072:    #\r\n2073:    # A HuMo beat past its cap therefore renders as real multi-clip coverage\r\n2074:    # now, each segment driven by its own slice of the line. This was the ONE\r\n2075:    # thing standing between the audio-driven lanes and the 45-word run: the\r\n2076:    # first campaign leg died here on `beat l001 needs 2 clips on humo (185\r\n2077:    # frames, cap 177)`.\r\n2078:    #\r\n2079:    # If per-segment slicing is ever removed, restore this refusal rather than\r\n2080:    # letting the beats through -- a split lip-synced beat with whole-line\r\n2081:    # audio is a sync defect that SHIPS, and nothing downstream would say so.\r\n2082:\r\n2083:    shot[\"coverage_plan\"] = plan.to_dict()\r\n2084:    # THE SIBLING RECEIPT (B3). Present only when the tier ceiling actually\r\n2085:    # narrowed something, and its ABSENCE is as load-bearing as its content:\r\n2086:    # ``render_driver.assert_coverage_plans`` re-derives this with the same\r\n2087:    # function and refuses on any difference, so a ceiling that appeared,\r\n2088:    # vanished or moved between plan time and render time is terminal rather\r\n2089:    # than silently re-planned. Stamped BEFORE the still-lane early return --\r\n2090:    # whether a lane owes stills has nothing to do with what it may render.\r\n2091:    receipt = _fc.coverage_contract_receipt(engine_id, declared,\r\n2092:                                            max_render_frames)\r\n2093:    if receipt is not None:\r\n2094:        shot[\"coverage_contract\"] = receipt\r\n2095:    if not _lane_consumes_a_still(shot, engine_id):\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
