{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_142","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$queries=@(@('\"'nodes/_otr_video_engines/eng_ghost_signal_official.py',55,125),@('nodes/_otr_video_engines/__init__.py',1,100)); foreach(\"'$q in $queries){$f=$q[0]; '\"'FILE '+\"'$f; $l=Get-Content -LiteralPath $f; for($i=$q[1];$i -le $q[2] -and $i -le $l.Count;$i++){'\"'{0}:{1}' -f \"'$i,$l[$i-1]}}'","aggregated_output":"FILE nodes/_otr_video_engines/eng_ghost_signal_official.py\r\n55:MM_V3_MIN_BYTES = 1_600_000_000\r\n56:\r\n57:#: The official v2 module. Balanced, and the only one of the three with\r\n58:#: MotionLoRA support (eight camera moves). Ghost wires no Motion LoRA today --\r\n59:#: that is excluded by the coding plan -- so this is a future capability, not a\r\n60:#: current one, and it is recorded rather than claimed.\r\n61:MM_V2_NAME = \"mm_sd_v15_v2.ckpt\"\r\n62:\r\n63:#: 1,817,888,431 bytes -- within 6 KB of mm-p_0.5, which is the clearest single\r\n64:#: piece of evidence that mm-p_0.5 is a v2 derivative.\r\n65:MM_V2_MIN_BYTES = 1_700_000_000\r\n66:\r\n67:\r\n68:# UNREGISTERED 2026-08-23. The class survives because the haunted lane inherits\r\n69:# it -- the v3 module, its byte floor and its recipe receipt are that lane's own\r\n70:# machinery. The public id `animatediff15_v3_video` is tombstoned in\r\n71:# RETIRED_ENGINE_IDS. Do not re-add @register to \"fix\" a missing engine.\r\n72:class GhostSignalV3Engine(GhostSignalEngine):\r\n73:    \"\"\"The official-v3 base. UNREGISTERED -- inherited by the haunted lane.\"\"\"\r\n74:\r\n75:    name = \"animatediff15_v3_video\"\r\n76:\r\n77:    motion_module_name = MM_V3_NAME\r\n78:    motion_min_bytes = MM_V3_MIN_BYTES\r\n79:    recipe_receipt_id = \"animatediff_sd15_v3_static16_512x288_v1\"\r\n80:\r\n81:    #: APACHE-2.0, AND THAT IS THE POINT OF THIS LANE. The code is Apache-2.0\r\n82:    #: and the SD1.5 checkpoint is CreativeML Open RAIL-M (hosted by Comfy-Org\r\n83:    #: themselves), so with a licensed motion module every artifact in the lane\r\n84:    #: is redistributable. The golden lane cannot say that.\r\n85:    #:\r\n86:    #: Still declared conservatively rather than True: `commercial_clean` is a\r\n87:    #: legal claim, RAIL-M carries use restrictions, and this build has not had\r\n88:    #: that reviewed. Apache-2.0 removes the BLOCKER; it does not by itself make\r\n89:    #: the lane commercially clean, and saying so would be exactly the kind of\r\n90:    #: overclaim the admission rules exist to stop.\r\n91:    commercial_clean = False\r\n92:\r\n93:\r\n94:#: The v3 DOMAIN ADAPTER -- a LoRA on the IMAGE model, not the motion module.\r\n95:#: 102,134,097 bytes, and the smallest artifact in this lane by two orders of\r\n96:#: magnitude.\r\n97:ADAPTER_V3_NAME = \"v3_sd15_adapter.ckpt\"\r\n98:\r\n99:#: G1.3: below its own artifact, and within 15% of it so a truncated fetch is\r\n100:#: still caught. 95 MB against a real 97.4 MB.\r\n101:ADAPTER_V3_MIN_BYTES = 95_000_000\r\n102:\r\n103:#: THE DIAL'S DIRECTION, and it is the opposite of what \"adapter\" suggests.\r\n104:#: Upstream trains this LoRA to ABSORB the video training set's own defects so\r\n105:#: they can be taken back out at inference: remove it, or scale it down, to get\r\n106:#: LESS of the dataset's grime. So 0.0 is the pristine image-model domain and\r\n107:#: 1.0 is the full video-dataset domain -- which is exactly the haunted end.\r\n108:#:\r\n109:#: 1.0 is the adapter's own full scale and therefore the honest default for a\r\n110:#: lane whose entire purpose is to be haunted. IT IS UNMEASURED: no strength\r\n111:#: has been qualified by eye yet, which is what the environment override below\r\n112:#: is for. Sweep it, look at the output, then freeze the number here.\r\n113:ADAPTER_V3_STRENGTH = 1.0\r\n114:\r\n115:#: The sweep knob, following the eng_fastwan_8gb recipe-override pattern.\r\n116:ADAPTER_V3_STRENGTH_ENV = \"OTR_GHOST_HAUNTED_LORA_STRENGTH\"\r\n117:\r\n118:\r\n119:@register\r\n120:class GhostSignalV3HauntedEngine(GhostSignalV3Engine):\r\n121:    \"\"\"``animatediff15_v3_haunted_video`` -- v3 plus the removable adapter.\r\n122:\r\n123:    A THIRD peer, additive exactly as v3 and v2 were. It inherits everything\r\n124:    from the clean v3 lane and adds one thing: the domain adapter on the MODEL\r\n125:    path. The clean v3 lane sits beside it as the reference and the golden lane\r\nFILE nodes/_otr_video_engines/__init__.py\r\n1:\"\"\"OTR video-engine namespace (the model-agnostic video adapter registry).\r\n2:\r\n3:A parallel namespace to ``nodes/_otr_audio_engines`` -- same proven pattern\r\n4:(AS-4), its OWN registry dict, zero cross-pollution with audio. Every video\r\n5:model (HuMo / LTX / Wan / lipsync / the cheap radio-floor families / the 3D\r\n6:Model Renderer / any \"+ Add Custom Model\") is a pluggable adapter the user\r\n7:selects PER ROLE; no model is \"primary\".\r\n8:\r\n9:Import-time is cold-import-clean (invariant V-12): importing this package +\r\n10::mod:`registry` + any adapter descriptor pulls in NO heavy lib (torch /\r\n11:transformers / diffusers) -- a ``test_cold_import_no_heavy_libs`` asserts it.\r\n12:Adapters lazy-import their frameworks inside ``load`` / ``render_clip``, never at\r\n13:module scope, so registering them here stays cold-import clean.\r\n14:\r\n15:---------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n16:HOW TO ADD YOUR OWN VIDEO ENGINE (same shape as the other three namespaces):\r\n17:---------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n18:\r\n19:The full checklist is docs/VIDEO_LANE_PREFLIGHT.md (enforced by\r\n20:tests/test_lane_preflight_matrix.py); EXTENDING_OTR.md gives the adapter\r\n21:walkthrough. One declaration deserves calling out here because silence about\r\n22:it is invisible until an episode quietly stops obeying the operator:\r\n23:\r\n24:  accepts_still -- DECLARE IT EXPLICITLY, True or False (preflight G3.6).\r\n25:  Every video lane is expected to render the still minted by whichever IMAGE\r\n26:  engine the operator selected for that role (the image-gen dropdowns beside\r\n27:  the video dropdowns on OTR_VideoDirector). Motion lanes inherit True from\r\n28:  MotionEngineBase; the procedural viz_* family declares False out loud\r\n29:  (no image gen exists for a visualizer). An engine that declares NEITHER\r\n30:  and lists no ``init_image`` resolves to False through a getattr fallback:\r\n31:  it mints no still, the operator's chosen image model is never invoked for\r\n32:  that role, and the episode renders anyway -- nothing reports it.\r\n33:  tests/test_still_spine_engine_coverage.py sweeps the live registry and\r\n34:  fails any engine that stays silent.\r\n35:\r\n36:And one more, if you build your lane as a SIBLING of an existing one:\r\n37:\r\n38:  EVERY PER-ARTIFACT CONSTANT MUST TRAVEL WITH THE LANE (preflight G1.3).\r\n39:  Model filename, byte floor, recipe receipt, quant token -- make each a CLASS\r\n40:  attribute your sibling can override, never a module-level constant read from\r\n41:  inside a method. A method reading the module constant means your lane loads\r\n42:  the PARENT's weights while stamping its own receipt, which is wrong pixels\r\n43:  under a confident label. This has now bitten twice here: once on the WAN\r\n44:  recipe accessors (see eng_fastwan_8gb) and once on Ghost, where the module\r\n45:  name had been made overridable and the byte floor beside it had not -- so a\r\n46:  byte-perfect 1.67 GB module was refused as \"truncated\" against a floor sized\r\n47:  for a 1.82 GB one. When you subclass, ask what ELSE was sized for the PARENT.\r\n48:\"\"\"\r\n49:\r\n50:# CW-4: register the cheap radio-floor families on package import so the platform\r\n51:# is non-empty (selectable per role) before any heavy engine exists. They are\r\n52:# cold-import clean (lazy ffmpeg/PIL/torch inside render_clip), so this import\r\n53:# pulls in nothing heavy (invariant V-12, the cold-import test). Guarded so a\r\n54:# packaging quirk never breaks the namespace import.\r\n55:try:  # pragma: no cover - trivial guard\r\n56:    from . import cheap_families as _cheap_families  # noqa: F401\r\n57:except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\r\n58:    pass\r\n59:\r\n60:# M2 / A-S5: register the in-process motion engine ltx_video (text->video).\r\n61:# This block registered TWO engines until 2026-08-26 -- wan_i2v (image->video)\r\n62:# was the other, and its retirement note is below. ltx_video is DEFAULT-OFF /\r\n63:# dark (empty default_roles + gated behind OTR_ENABLE_LTX_VIDEO) so it shows in\r\n64:# the static per-role dropdown (V-6) but is never a default and fails closed\r\n65:# until the operator enables it AND the wrapper + checkpoints are\r\n66:# installed/verified on the GPU box. Cold-import clean (lazy LTX wrapper +\r\n67:# torch inside\r\n68:# load/render_clip, never here), so this import pulls in nothing heavy (invariant\r\n69:# V-12, the cold-import test). Guarded so a packaging quirk never breaks the\r\n70:# namespace import.\r\n71:try:  # pragma: no cover - trivial guard\r\n72:    from . import eng_ltx_video as _eng_ltx_video  # noqa: F401\r\n73:except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\r\n74:    pass\r\n75:\r\n76:# wan_i2v RETIRED 2026-08-26 -- 19.82 GiB of weights against a 14.5 GiB\r\n77:# target; it only ran by offloading (120 min TIMEOUT vs 48.5 for the 5B\r\n78:# wan_ti2v that replaces it). Tombstoned in\r\n79:# _otr_shared/public_engines.RETIRED_ENGINE_IDS so a saved graph naming it\r\n80:# gets a NAMED retirement refusal, not \"no such engine\".\r\n81:\r\n82:# GO_FORWARD 4A (2026-06-14): register the Wan2.2 TI2V-5B 8GB-tier engine. Like\r\n83:# wan_i2v it is DEFAULT-OFF / dark (empty default_roles + gated behind\r\n84:# OTR_ENABLE_WAN_TI2V) and fails closed until the GGUF + the Wan2.2 VAE are on\r\n85:# disk. Its 5B core node class (Wan22ImageToVideoLatent) was captured from a live\r\n86:# /object_info before coding. Cold-import clean (V-12); guarded so a packaging\r\n87:# quirk never breaks the namespace import.\r\n88:try:  # pragma: no cover - trivial guard\r\n89:    from . import eng_wan_ti2v as _eng_wan_ti2v  # noqa: F401\r\n90:except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\r\n91:    pass\r\n92:\r\n93:# video-tiers (2026-07-20): register the 8GB-tier LTX-Video 0.9.8 distilled 2B I2V\r\n94:# engine (ltx_8gb). Unlike the older dark motion engines it is a NORMAL selectable\r\n95:# row -- requires_flag=None, empty default_roles (selectable, not a default); no\r\n96:# enable flag (registry IS the menu). It fails CLOSED (ordinary asset preflight) until\r\n97:# the 0.9.8 checkpoint + the shared t5xxl_fp16 are on disk. Its 0.9.8 core node graph\r\n98:# was captured from a live /object_info + a functional in-process smoke before coding.\r\n99:# Cold-import clean (V-12: lazy LTX core nodes + torch inside load/render_clip).\r\n100:# Guarded so a packaging quirk never breaks the namespace import.\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
